 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nMySQL index constraint parsing fails with UnboundLocalError\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen parsing MySQL CREATE TABLE statements with index constraints that include certain options like COMMENT, VISIBLE/INVISIBLE, or ENGINE_ATTRIBUTE, the parser throws an UnboundLocalError for the variable 'opt'.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\n\n# This should parse successfully but throws UnboundLocalError\nsql = \"CREATE TABLE foo (a BIGINT, INDEX b USING HASH (c) COMMENT 'd' VISIBLE ENGINE_ATTRIBUTE = 'e' WITH PARSER foo)\"\nsqlglot.parse_one(sql, dialect=\"mysql\")\n```\n\nThe error occurs when trying to parse index constraints with options like:\n- `COMMENT 'some comment'`\n- `VISIBLE` or `INVISIBLE` \n- `ENGINE_ATTRIBUTE = 'value'`\n- `SECONDARY_ENGINE_ATTRIBUTE = 'value'`\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nThe parser should successfully parse MySQL CREATE TABLE statements with index constraints containing these options and generate the appropriate AST.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\nUnboundLocalError is raised because the `opt` variable is referenced before assignment in the index constraint parsing logic.\n</issue>\n",
